{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "7c1f0a52-6d3b-4a19-9f42-0b8e5d3c1a70",
    "name": "WikiStream Go (ch-4) API Tests",
    "description": "End-to-end flow against the ch-4 Go service on :7001.\n\nRoutes are registered in internal/httpapi/api.go and are NOT versioned — there is no /v1 prefix (unlike the Kotlin service).\n\nPublic:    GET /status, POST /auth/register, POST /auth/login\nProtected: GET /stats, POST /auth/logout  (Bearer token via auth.Guard)\n\nRun the whole collection in order with the Collection Runner: `Register User` mints a unique TEST_EMAIL each run, so the suite is re-runnable without 409s, and `Login` captures ACCESS_TOKEN for the protected calls.\n\nErrors all share one shape: {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}.\n\nThere is no rate limiting: the per-IP limiter and the bcrypt semaphore were removed from api.go as workshop noise, so no request here can return 429.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "BASE_URL",
      "value": "http://localhost:7001",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "TEST_EMAIL",
      "value": "go-ch4@example.test",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "TEST_PASSWORD",
      "value": "correct-horse-battery",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "ACCESS_TOKEN",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "EXPIRES_IN",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "LOGIN_AT",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health Check",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{BASE_URL}}/status",
          "host": ["{{BASE_URL}}"],
          "path": ["status"]
        },
        "description": "Public. handleStatus returns a fixed body with no dependencies, so it answers 200 on both the in-memory and the Cassandra backend."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('content-type is JSON', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/json'));",
              "pm.test('body is {\"status\":\"ok\"}', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('ok'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Register User",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{TEST_EMAIL}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{TEST_PASSWORD}}\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{BASE_URL}}/auth/register",
          "host": ["{{BASE_URL}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "register"]
        },
        "description": "Public. Returns 201 with {\"status\":\"registered\"} — note it does NOT return a token; you must log in separately.\n\nThe pre-request script mints a unique address each run so re-running the collection does not collide with an account already in Cassandra."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Unique per run: with the Cassandra backend, accounts survive restarts,",
              "// so a fixed address would 409 on the second run.",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('TEST_EMAIL', `go-ch4-${Date.now()}@example.test`);"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "pm.test('body reports registered', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('registered'));",
              "pm.test('no token is issued by register', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.not.have.property('access_token'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Register Duplicate (expect 409)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{TEST_EMAIL}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{TEST_PASSWORD}}\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{BASE_URL}}/auth/register",
          "host": ["{{BASE_URL}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "register"]
        },
        "description": "Same address again. CreateUser returns ConflictError -> 409. This one deliberately leaks that the email exists; login does not. The trade-off is documented in auth.Register — and is now unbounded, since the rate limiter that used to slow bulk enumeration was removed."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
              "pm.test('code is CONFLICT_ERROR', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('CONFLICT_ERROR'));",
              "pm.test('message is generic', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('email already registered'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Register Weak Password (expect 400)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"weak-{{$timestamp}}@example.test\",\n  \"password\": \"short\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{BASE_URL}}/auth/register",
          "host": ["{{BASE_URL}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "register"]
        },
        "description": "validatePassword enforces 8..72 bytes (72 is bcrypt's own input limit). Five characters is a ValidationError -> 400."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
              "pm.test('code is VALIDATION_ERROR', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('VALIDATION_ERROR'));",
              "pm.test('message names the length rule', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.include('password must be 8..72 bytes'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Login",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{TEST_EMAIL}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{TEST_PASSWORD}}\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{BASE_URL}}/auth/login",
          "host": ["{{BASE_URL}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "login"]
        },
        "description": "Public. Returns auth.TokenResponse: access_token, token_type (\"Bearer\") and expires_in — seconds remaining, not a timestamp. Captures both into collection variables for the protected calls below."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test('token_type is Bearer', () => pm.expect(body.token_type).to.eql('Bearer'));",
              "pm.test('access_token is a three-part JWT', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "  pm.expect(body.access_token.split('.')).to.have.lengthOf(3);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('expires_in is seconds remaining, not a timestamp', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.expires_in).to.be.a('number');",
              "  pm.expect(body.expires_in).to.be.above(0);",
              "  // ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL defaults to 1h; anything near epoch-seconds means",
              "  // the handler regressed to returning a timestamp.",
              "  pm.expect(body.expires_in).to.be.below(90000);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('ACCESS_TOKEN', body.access_token);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('EXPIRES_IN', body.expires_in);",
              "// Lets the revocation check below prove the token was still alive when",
              "// it was refused, without having to decode the JWT.",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('LOGIN_AT', Date.now());"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Login Wrong Password (expect 401)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{TEST_EMAIL}}\",\n  \"password\": \"definitely-not-the-password\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{BASE_URL}}/auth/login",
          "host": ["{{BASE_URL}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "login"]
        },
        "description": "A real account with a bad password. writeError answers a single generic message on purpose — it must never reveal which check failed, so this is indistinguishable from an unknown address."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
              "pm.test('code is UNAUTHORIZED_ERROR', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('UNAUTHORIZED_ERROR'));",
              "pm.test('message does not reveal which check failed', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('invalid credentials'));",
              "pm.test('WWW-Authenticate header is set (RFC 7235)', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('WWW-Authenticate')).to.include('Bearer'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Fetch Stats (with token)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}" }],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{BASE_URL}}/stats",
          "host": ["{{BASE_URL}}"],
          "path": ["stats"]
        },
        "description": "Protected. Reads the live in-memory counters on BOTH backends — a single response cannot tell you which backend is active; only a restart can."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const s = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test('snapshot has every counter', () => {",
              "  ['total_messages', 'distinct_users', 'bot_edits', 'human_edits'].forEach(k => {",
              "    pm.expect(s, k).to.have.property(k);",
              "    pm.expect(s[k], k).to.be.a('number');",
              "  });",
              "  pm.expect(s).to.have.property('by_server_url');",
              "  pm.expect(s).to.have.property('last_event');",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('bot + human edits do not exceed total', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(s.bot_edits + s.human_edits).to.be.at.most(s.total_messages));",
              "",
              "// Informational: the consumer needs a moment after startup before the",
              "// Wikimedia stream produces anything, so zero here is not a failure.",
              "if (s.total_messages === 0) {",
              "  console.log('total_messages is 0 — consumer may still be warming up');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Fetch Stats without token (expect 401)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{BASE_URL}}/stats",
          "host": ["{{BASE_URL}}"],
          "path": ["stats"]
        },
        "description": "No Authorization header at all. auth.Guard fails closed: any route not listed in the public map needs a token, so a route added without updating that map ends up protected rather than open."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
              "pm.test('code is UNAUTHORIZED_ERROR', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('UNAUTHORIZED_ERROR'));",
              "pm.test('WWW-Authenticate advertises the Bearer realm', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('WWW-Authenticate')).to.eql('Bearer realm=\"ch-4\"'));",
              "pm.test('no stats leak in the error body', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.not.have.property('total_messages'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Logout",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}" }],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{BASE_URL}}/auth/logout",
          "host": ["{{BASE_URL}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "logout"]
        },
        "description": "Protected, and takes no body — the jti to revoke comes from the token's own claims. Answers 204 with an empty body.\n\nThe revocation row carries a TTL derived from the token's exp, so it self-deletes once the token would have expired anyway."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204 No Content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));",
              "pm.test('body is empty', () => pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.be.empty);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Verify Revoked Token (expect 401)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}" }],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{BASE_URL}}/stats",
          "host": ["{{BASE_URL}}"],
          "path": ["stats"]
        },
        "description": "The same token that worked three requests ago. It is still cryptographically valid and unexpired — it is refused purely because logout recorded its jti in the revocation store. This is the one assertion that proves revocation actually works."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
              "pm.test('code is UNAUTHORIZED_ERROR', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('UNAUTHORIZED_ERROR'));",
              "pm.test('token itself is unexpired — refusal is due to revocation', () => {",
              "  const issuedAt = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('LOGIN_AT'));",
              "  const ttlMs = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('EXPIRES_IN')) * 1000;",
              "  pm.expect(issuedAt + ttlMs, 'token should not have expired on its own')",
              "    .to.be.above(Date.now());",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
